Data sources

Data is fetched at runtime directly from the providers; none of it is part of
the Software or covered by the MIT License in LICENSE, and each provider's
terms apply.

- CoinGecko (market data, coin and exchange logos): "Powered by CoinGecko"
  (https://www.coingecko.com), as required by the CoinGecko API terms.
- Coin Metrics Community API (on-chain values): licensed under Creative
  Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 (CC BY-NC 4.0). Non-commercial use
  only: a fork that is monetised (paid app, ads, subscriptions) must not use
  this source without its own license from Coin Metrics.
- alternative.me (Crypto Fear & Greed Index).
- European Central Bank (www.ecb.europa.eu, data-api.ecb.europa.eu): euro
  foreign exchange reference rates. Source: ECB. Rates for a base other than
  EUR (cross rates, 5 significant digits) and the change against the previous
  ECB day are calculated by the apps from these rates. Terms:
  https://www.ecb.europa.eu/services/using-our-site/disclaimer/html/index.en.html
- National Bank of Ukraine (bank.gov.ua): official exchange rates of the
  hryvnia, for currencies the ECB does not list. Source: National Bank of
  Ukraine. Rates against USD and EUR (cross rates, 5 significant digits) and the
  change against the previous publication are calculated by the apps.
- National Bank of Poland (api.nbp.pl): average exchange rates of tables A and B,
  for the remaining currencies. Source: Narodowy Bank Polski. Rates against USD
  and EUR (cross rates of the same publication date, 5 significant digits) and
  the change against the previous week's table are calculated by the apps.
- ExchangeRate-API (open.er-api.com, fallback FX rates): "Rates By Exchange
  Rate API" (https://www.exchangerate-api.com).
- Exchanges and other price sources named in the privacy policy (for example
  Binance), each under its own API terms.

